    tools: preflight + parallel-GPU mode for the autonomous v2 run
    
    preflight_v2.py runs in the parent shell BEFORE the runner detaches, so
    blocking problems surface in the terminal in ~10s instead of 12 hours
    later. Hard-checks the failure modes that would silently ruin an
    unattended run on a fresh box: git identity and `git push` auth (without
    which every 20-min checkpoint commits locally and never reaches the
    remote -- a box crash would then lose everything), torch/CUDA with
    native sm_120 Blackwell kernels, bitsandbytes (the N6 4-bit arm aborts
    without it), access to the GATED mistralai/Mistral-Small-Instruct-2409,
    ~80GB free disk for weights, and the 52 analyzed cells N1/N4 read.
    
    V2_PARALLEL_GPU=1 runs N5 and N6 concurrently: peak ~52GB (Mistral-22B
    bf16 @batch16 + KV) + ~19GB (Qwen-7B bf16 @batch32) = ~71GB of the 96GB
    card, separate CUDA contexts => identical results, ~14h -> ~8h wall
    clock. Explicitly documented (in code and protocol doc) that batch size,
    attention impl, and dtype must NOT be retuned for throughput: they are
    the held-constant variables, N5's control arm IS the recorded cell, and
    N6 exists to remove a batch/code/hardware confound.
    
    Both modes re-verified end-to-end against the stubbed-collector harness
    with a real bare remote: detach, per-stage + 20-min checkpoint commits
    all pushed (git lock correctly serializes the concurrent stages in
    parallel mode), success-checkers emitting pre-registered verdicts, final
    results commit, noise files untracked.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

